<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kruševo Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1903 CE – 1903 CE · capital Kruševo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ten-day revolutionary government in the mountain town of Kruševo during the Ilinden Uprising of 1903, celebrated in North Macedonia as a founding moment.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 2 August 1903, the feast of Saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elijah">Elijah</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/internal-macedonian-revolutionary-organization">Internal Macedonian-Adrianople Revolutionary Organisation</a> launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilinden-preobrazhenie-uprising">Ilinden Uprising</a> against Ottoman rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>. Rebels under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-karev">Nikola Karev</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitu-guli">Pitu Guli</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krusevo">Kruševo</a>, a prosperous mountain town of Slav, Aromanian and Greek-oriented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> families, and proclaimed a provisional government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-karev">Karev</a> headed a council that included members of the different communities, and the town's administration, courts and supplies were reorganised for defence. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krusevo-manifesto">Kruševo Manifesto</a>, attributed to the rebels, called on the local Muslim population to join the struggle against tyranny rather than against neighbours. The republic lasted about ten days.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>An Ottoman army retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krusevo">Kruševo</a> around 12 August 1903; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitu-guli">Pitu Guli</a> died defending the Mečkin Kamen position and much of the town was burnt. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a> both claim the uprising, and the Ilinden memorial at Kruševo is a national symbol of North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/krusevo-republic.jpg" alt="Kruševo Republic" width="320" height="193"><figcaption>Image: MacedonianBoy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kru%C5%A1evo_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1903 CE – 1903 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kruševo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nikola Karev</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bulgarian, Macedonian, Aromanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Krushevo Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1903&amp;focus=krusevo-republic" aria-label="Kruševo Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5199 703 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kruševo Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5519 959L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5519 959h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5519 959h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kruševo. <a href="/atlas?year=1903&amp;focus=krusevo-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
